.TH STLAB 1 "September 27, 2026" "Spacetime Lab" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
stlab \- relativity demos and N-body gravity sandbox
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stlab
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B stlab
runs ten deterministic relativity scenario presets with a 60 frames-per-second
frame loop, an interactive N-body gravity sandbox
.RB ( \-\-sandbox ),
a real Solar System simulator built on JPL Horizons ephemerides
.RB ( \-\-space ),
and a cinematic binary black hole merger view
.RB ( \-\-merger ).
It renders an ASCII live view on a terminal, and can export
deterministic CSV time series and P6 PPM raster images.
On macOS the sandbox can also run in a native window
.RB ( \-\-visual );
a headless visual framebuffer render to PPM works on every platform
.RB ( \-\-visual\-shot ).
The
.B \-\-space
and
.B \-\-merger
views open a native window by default on macOS
.RB ( \-\-visual
is accepted but not required) and run headless under
.B \-\-visual\-shot
or
.BR \-\-movie .
.PP
Physics uses SI doubles throughout (meters, kilograms, seconds, radians)
with seeded random number generators only.
The same command line arguments produce byte-identical CSV and PPM files.
.PP
With no flags,
.B stlab
starts the
.I twin
scenario interactively when standard input is a terminal,
and falls back to a headless batch run otherwise.
.SH OPTIONS
All value flags accept both
.BI "\-\-flag " value
and
.BI "\-\-flag=" value
forms.
.TP
.BI "\-\-scenario " name|all
Scenario preset:
.BR twin ,
.BR pole ,
.BR doppler ,
.BR mercury ,
.BR gps ,
.BR bend ,
.BR ring ,
.BR flamm ,
.BR chirp ,
.BR shadow ,
or
.B all
for every preset in that order.
Default is
.BR twin .
A bare
.B \-\-smoke
run without
.B \-\-scenario
runs
.BR all .
Unknown names fail with exit status 2.
.TP
.BI "\-\-frames " N
Frames per scenario, an integer 0 to 1000000.
Default is 600 (10 seconds at 60 fps).
Without an explicit
.B \-\-frames ,
.B \-\-smoke
uses 1 frame per scenario, and sandbox smoke uses 60.
When a run outlasts a preset frame count, the preset loops deterministically.
In interactive mode
.B \-\-frames
caps the session length instead.
.TP
.BI "\-\-ppm " path
PPM output path.
For one scenario the path is used verbatim as the output file.
When the scenario set is
.B all ,
the path names a directory and each scenario is written as
.IB path /<scen>.ppm
(parent directories must already exist).
Without
.B \-\-ppm ,
no PPM file is written.
Sandbox interactive export defaults to
.IR sandbox.ppm .
.TP
.BI "\-\-csv " path
CSV output path, with the same file-or-directory rule as
.BR \-\-ppm .
Without
.B \-\-csv ,
no CSV file is written.
Sandbox interactive export defaults to
.IR sandbox.csv .
.TP
.B \-\-sandbox
Run the N-body sandbox mode instead of the scenario presets.
Uses
.B \-\-preset
and
.B \-\-seed
below; interactive on a terminal, headless batch with
.B \-\-smoke
or when standard input is not a terminal.
.TP
.BI "\-\-preset " N
Preset index for the selected mode. With
.BR \-\-sandbox ,
index 0 to 3:
.B 0
solar (free Sun plus 8 planets),
.B 1
binary (two 1e30 kg stars plus a planet),
.B 2
hole_disk (fixed 10 solar-mass hole plus a seeded 24-particle ring and probe),
.B 3
slingshot (fixed Jupiter-mass planet plus a probe).
With
.BR \-\-merger ,
index 0 to 3 selects the binary: 0 GW150914-like 36+29 Msun,
1 equal mass 30+30 Msun, 2 unequal q = 3 (30+10 Msun),
3 extreme q = 8 (24+3 Msun).
With
.BR \-\-space ,
index 0 to 5 selects the scenario: 0 Solar System at J2000.0,
1 Solar System today, 2 Sun replaced by a 1 Msun black hole,
3 rogue 10 Msun black-hole flyby, 4 Earth swarm (2000 Earths at 1 AU),
5 black hole plus 1,000,000 test Earths.
Default is 0.
Out-of-range values fail with exit status 2.
.TP
.BI "\-\-seed " N
Unsigned integer seed for sandbox preset generation.
Default is 20260927.
Same preset plus same seed gives the same initial state.
.TP
.BI "\-\-integrator " verlet|rk4
Sandbox stepper: velocity Verlet (default) or classic 4th-order
Runge-Kutta. The RK4 stepper itself performs no collision pass and no
speed cap; the application runs the shared post-step pass
(merge/bounce collision resolution plus the speed cap) after every
RK4 step, so both integrators apply identical collision and cap
policy -- only the stepping scheme differs. The interactive header
and the headless summary line report the active stepper as
integ=verlet or integ=rk4. Other values fail with exit status 2.
.TP
.B \-\-visual
With
.BR \-\-sandbox :
run the sandbox in a native window instead of the character-grid
terminal view. With
.B \-\-merger
or
.BR \-\-space
it is accepted but not required (those views window by default).
macOS only -- AppKit driven through the Objective-C
runtime with system frameworks, no third-party dependencies; on other
platforms it prints "stlab: --visual needs macOS (AppKit)" and exits 1.
The software rasterizer draws a 1280x800 framebuffer (shaded body
discs, fading trails, starfield, HUD) with the same keys and spawn
form as the terminal screen.
.B \-\-frames
caps the session length;
.B \-\-smoke
is ignored.
.TP
.BI "\-\-visual\-shot " path
With
.BR \-\-sandbox :
headless visual render -- steps the sim
.B \-\-frames
frames (default 60), then writes the final 1280x800 framebuffer as a
P6 PPM to
.IR path .
No window and no pacing; works on every platform; identical arguments
produce a byte-identical file. When both visual flags are given,
.B \-\-visual\-shot
takes precedence. Without
.BR \-\-sandbox ,
.BR \-\-merger ,
or
.BR \-\-space ,
both visual flags are ignored. With
.B \-\-merger
or
.B \-\-space
it renders the last of
.B \-\-frames
frames (default 600) of the merger or space view to
.IR path .
.TP
.B \-\-merger
Cinematic binary black hole merger view: a Peters 0PN inspiral
timeline, shaped plunge, damped-sinusoid ringdown, and
remnant/QNM fits drive a rendered spacetime sheet rippled by the
retarded-time quadrupole strain.
.B \-\-preset
0 to 3 selects the binary (see above). Opens a window by default;
.B \-\-visual\-shot
or
.B \-\-movie
run headless. See
.IR doc/MERGER.md .
.TP
.B \-\-space
Full space simulator: the real Solar System from NASA JPL Horizons
state vectors (J2000 or today's epoch), Newtonian N-body plus a 1PN
correction, J2/J4 zonal harmonics, collisions, tidal disruption and
black-hole capture, time warp in both directions with checkpoint-exact
rewind, and a console for sandbox edits.
.B \-\-preset
0 to 5 selects the scenario (see above). Opens a window by default;
.B \-\-visual\-shot
or
.B \-\-movie
run headless. See
.IR doc/SPACE.md .
.TP
.BI "\-\-movie " dir
With
.B \-\-merger
or
.B \-\-space
headless: write a PPM frame sequence
.RI ( merger_NNNNN.ppm
or
.RI space_NNNNN.ppm )
to
.IR dir ;
parent directories must already exist.
.TP
.BI "\-\-movie\-every " N
Frame stride for
.BR \-\-movie ,
an integer >= 1 (default 2): every Nth frame is written.
.TP
.B \-\-smoke
Headless run: no raw-mode user interface, no pacing unless configured,
prints one summary line per scenario (or sandbox run) and exits.
.TP
.B \-\-list
Print the ten scenario preset names, one per line, and exit 0.
.TP
.B \-\-help
.TQ
.B \-h
Print the built-in help text and exit 0.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-adapt
Disable 60 fps frame pacing; run as fast as possible.
Output bytes are unchanged.
.SH KEYS
Interactive screens use raw-mode single-key input (no Enter needed).
.SS Scenario screen
.TP
.B W S
(or up/down arrows) orbit the camera pitch up/down.
.TP
.B A D
(or left/right arrows) orbit the camera yaw left/right.
.TP
.B "+ = R"
Zoom the camera in;
.B "\- _ F"
zoom out.
.TP
.B 1\-9 0
Switch scenario: 1 to 9 select presets 1 to 9, 0 selects preset 10
.RB ( shadow ).
Resets the frame counter.
.TP
.B P
Pause or resume stepping.
.TP
.B E
Export the current frame: one CSV row plus one PPM view.
Uses the
.B \-\-csv
and
.B \-\-ppm
paths with the single-scenario rule (defaults
.IB <scen>.csv
and
.IB <scen>.ppm ).
.TP
.B Q
Quit.
Escape and Ctrl-C also quit.
.SS Sandbox screen
.TP
.B W S
(or up/down arrows) orbit the camera pitch up/down.
.TP
.B A D
(or left/right arrows) orbit the camera yaw left/right.
.TP
.B "+ = R"
Zoom the camera in;
.B "\- _ F"
zoom out.
.TP
.B Tab
Cycle the follow target: centroid, then body 0 through body n-1.
.TP
.B N
Open the spawn-body form.
The form is prefilled with a probe on a circular orbit about body 0
through the view center.
.TP
.B K
Remove the followed body (compacts the body list, clears trails).
.TP
.B G
Load the next preset (solar, binary, hole_disk, slingshot, wrapping around).
Resets the follow target and clears trails.
.TP
.B Z X
Halve (Z) or double (X) the integration step dt, clamped to 1e-6 s
through 1e9 s. The default dt is 1000 s.
.TP
.B C
Cycle the time warp: 1, 10, then 100 integrator steps per frame.
.TP
.B T
Toggle orbit trails (ring buffer, depth 128) on or off.
Turning trails off clears them.
.TP
.B D
Visual mode only: toggle the spacetime-grid sheet and its orientation
aids (x/y/z axis triad, 100 px scale bar with auto m/km/AU units).
The sheet extends toward the horizon -- a uniform core lattice
continues with geometrically spaced lines far out -- and is an
ILLUSTRATIVE potential-shaped dent
(h = \-K * sum w_i s^2/(d_i^2 + s^2) in the orbital plane, mass weights
w_i = (m_i/M_max)^0.25, kernel width and depth set in view units),
not the spacetime metric, and has no effect on the physics.
In visual mode
.B D
takes over the WASD yaw-right binding; the Right arrow still yaws.
.TP
.B P
Pause or resume stepping.
.TP
.B E
Export the body snapshot CSV plus the current PPM view.
Uses the
.B \-\-csv
and
.B \-\-ppm
paths, defaulting to
.I sandbox.csv
and
.IR sandbox.ppm .
.TP
.B ?
Toggle the built-in key help (press
.B ?
again or any other handled key path to return).
.TP
.B Q
Quit.
Escape and Ctrl-C also quit.
.SS Spawn form
.TP
.B up down
Move between the eleven fields: name, mass_kg, radius_m, px_m, py_m, pz_m,
vx_m_s, vy_m_s, vz_m_s, fixed, SPAWN>.
.TP
.B typing
Printable characters append to the current field; backspace (DEL or Ctrl-H)
deletes one character.
Numbers accept forms such as 1.989e30; the fixed field accepts y or n.
.TP
.B Enter
Advance to the next field; pressing Enter on SPAWN> validates and spawns
the body (mass must be positive, radius non-negative, positions and
velocities numeric). The new body becomes the follow target.
.TP
.B Esc
Cancel without spawning.
.SS "Space and merger screens"
The
.B \-\-space
and
.B \-\-merger
views (windowed on macOS, or headless frame output) have their own key
maps -- warp ladder, camera, console commands, and view toggles --
documented in
.I doc/SPACE.md
and
.I doc/MERGER.md .
.SH FILES
.SS Scenario CSV
Headless scenario runs append one row per frame.
The header line is:
.PP
.RS 4
frame,t_s,x_m,y_m,z_m,q,obs0,obs1,obs2,obs3,obs4,obs5,obs6,obs7
.RE
.PP
Columns are the frame index, sim time in seconds, head position in meters,
head observable, then all eight observable slots in SI units
(see the per-preset observable labels printed by the interactive screen).
Values use %.17g formatting, comma-separated, one row per frame.
Interactive
.B E
writes the same header plus the single current-frame row.
.SS Sandbox headless CSV
Sandbox batch runs write a time-series energy log with the header:
.PP
.RS 4
frame,t_s,E_J,n
.RE
.PP
Columns are the frame index, sim time in seconds, total system energy in
joules, and live body count.
.SS Sandbox body-snapshot CSV
Sandbox interactive
.B E
writes a one-row-per-body snapshot.
The first line is
.IB t_s= <time>
and the second line is the header:
.PP
.RS 4
name,m_kg,r_m,px_m,py_m,pz_m,vx_m_s,vy_m_s,vz_m_s,fixed
.RE
.PP
Body names are sanitized on spawn (commas, quotes, and newlines become
spaces) so rows stay parseable.
Masses are kilograms, radii and positions meters, velocities meters per
second; fixed is 1 for fixed bodies, 0 otherwise.
.SS PPM raster
All PPM exports are binary P6 format: a
.I P6
magic line, a size line
.RI ( "320 200"
for scenario and terminal-sandbox exports,
.I "1280 800"
for
.BR \-\-visual\-shot ),
a
.I 255
maxval line, then width*height RGB byte triples, top row first.
Scenario views paint phosphor points plus an amber path over dim axes;
sandbox views paint the followed body bright, fixed bodies amber, free
bodies white, and dim trail polylines.
.SH EXAMPLES
List the scenario presets:
.PP
.RS 4
stlab \-\-list
.RE
.PP
Run every scenario headless, 60 frames each, fastest:
.PP
.RS 4
stlab \-\-scenario all \-\-frames 60 \-\-ppm /tmp \-\-csv /tmp
.br
\-\-smoke \-\-no\-adapt
.RE
.PP
Run one scenario interactively when standard input is a terminal:
.PP
.RS 4
stlab \-\-scenario twin \-\-frames 600
.RE
.PP
Run the sandbox on the binary preset:
.PP
.RS 4
stlab \-\-sandbox \-\-preset 1
.RE
.PP
Run every sandbox preset headless with exports:
.PP
.RS 4
for p in 0 1 2 3; do stlab \-\-sandbox \-\-preset $p \-\-frames 60
.br
\-\-ppm /tmp/sbx/p$p.ppm \-\-csv /tmp/sbx/p$p.csv \-\-smoke \-\-no\-adapt; done
.RE
.PP
Open the sandbox in a native window (macOS only):
.PP
.RS 4
stlab \-\-sandbox \-\-preset 0 \-\-visual
.RE
.PP
Render the visual view headless to a 1280x800 PPM (any platform):
.PP
.RS 4
stlab \-\-sandbox \-\-preset 0 \-\-frames 60 \-\-visual\-shot /tmp/vis.ppm
.RE
.PP
Open the space simulator on today's Solar System (macOS), or render it
headless elsewhere:
.PP
.RS 4
stlab \-\-space \-\-preset 1
.br
stlab \-\-space \-\-preset 0 \-\-frames 300 \-\-visual\-shot /tmp/s.ppm
.RE
.PP
Render a merger movie frame sequence and a final still:
.PP
.RS 4
stlab \-\-merger \-\-preset 0 \-\-frames 2400 \-\-movie /tmp/f
.br
\-\-movie\-every 2
.RE
.SH "MAKE TARGETS"
Convenience wrappers around the options above (see the Makefile):
.TP
.B make merger
Build
.B stlab
and run
.BR "\-\-merger \-\-visual"
(macOS window).
.TP
.B make merger-shot
Render a 700-frame merger still to
.IR build/merger/shot.ppm .
.TP
.B make space
Run
.B \-\-space
windowed (macOS).
.TP
.B make space-shot
Render a 300-frame space still to
.IR build/space/shot.ppm .
.TP
.B make ephem-accuracy
Run
.BR "stephem \-\-accuracy" :
integrate the catalog from J2000 to today and compare every body
against its fetched Horizons vector. Slow; deliberately not part of
.BR "make verify" .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success: help or list printed, batch run completed, or interactive session
quit normally.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime failure: scenario or preset setup failed, a step failed, or a CSV
or PPM path could not be written.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: unknown flag, missing flag value, bad
.B \-\-frames ,
.B \-\-preset ,
.B \-\-seed ,
or
.B \-\-integrator ,
unknown scenario name, or bad preset index.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR stverify (1),
.BR sttest (1),
.BR stsolar (1),
.BR stfuzz (1),
.BR stbench (1),
.BR stspace (1),
.BR stephem (1)
.PP
Project files: README.md, CONTRACT.md, doc/PHYSICS.md, doc/SPACE.md,
doc/MERGER.md, doc/CAPABILITY.md.
.SH NOTES
Determinism: identical arguments (including
.B \-\-seed
for sandbox presets) produce byte-identical CSV and PPM files.
Frame pacing
.RB ( \-\-no\-adapt )
changes wall-clock timing only, never output bytes.
All physics quantities are SI doubles; only the camera projection is
normalized into a unitless view box.
